                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1138/18: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gross</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-03-17T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 17,
                                1927—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 18—10:15
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>17. Haitian Minister to Santo Domingo has telegraphed to President Borno that
                    Senator King has decided not to enter Haiti. The incident appears closed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gross</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
